The error message said: duplicated label &#39;Problem4.3.3&#39;<br><br>You should make sure the chunk labels are unique, as documented in<br><a href="http://yihui.name/knitr/options" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://yihui.name/knitr/options&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792355998471000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0mPiUxsTbm6Pl5UtvdgnRd">http://yihui.name/knitr/options</a><br><br>Regards,<br>Yihui<br>--<br>Yihui Xie &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">xiey...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>Phone: <a href="tel:(515)%20294-2465" value="+15152942465" target="_blank" rel="nofollow">515-294-2465</a> Web: <a href="http://yihui.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://yihui.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792355998471000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2SOWwtms4FAs0JjgeOXTb9">http://yihui.name</a><br>Department of Statistics, Iowa State University<br>2215 Snedecor Hall, Ames, IA<br><br><br>On Fri, Dec 28, 2012 at 5:56 AM,  &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">pradip...@samhsa.hhs.gov</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Hello,<br>&gt;<br>&gt; When running the code chunk-wise, I have not encountered any error.  But<br>&gt; when I attempted to run all chunks at a time, I got the following error (at<br>&gt; the very last code chunk), which is not intelligible to me (beginner knitr<br>&gt; user). Please note that I got the Sweave code (Rnw file) from the following<br>&gt; site:<br>&gt; <a href="http://isites.harvard.edu/icb/icb.do?keyword=k76038&amp;pageid=icb.page398554" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://isites.harvard.edu/icb/icb.do?keyword%3Dk76038%26pageid%3Dicb.page398554&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792355998471000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0mLmqahAu-3oRjguMRd1aQ">http://isites.harvard.edu/icb/icb.do?keyword=k76038&amp;pageid=icb.page398554</a>.<br>&gt; I would appreciate receiving any help you may provide toward resolving the<br>&gt; issue.<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Thanks,<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Pradip Muhuri<br>&gt;<br>&gt; #### Error below<br>&gt;<br>&gt; processing file: practice1.Rnw<br>&gt; Error in parse_block(g) : duplicated label &#39;Problem4.3.3&#39;<br>&gt; Calls: knit ... process_file -&gt; split_file -&gt; lapply -&gt; FUN -&gt; parse_block<br>&gt; Execution halted<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt; ###### My reproducible example is appended below<br>&gt;<br>&gt; \documentclass[11pt]{article}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; \usepackage{verbatim,array,multicol,palatino,enumerate}<br>&gt; \usepackage{amsmath,amsfonts}<br>&gt; \usepackage{latexsym}<br>&gt; %\usepackage[pdftex]{color}<br>&gt; %\usepackage[pdftex]{geometry}<br>&gt; %\usepackage[pdftex]{graphicx}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; \usepackage{Sweave}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; %\usepackage[pdftex,colorlinks=true,menucolor=red,urlcolor=blue]{hyperref}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; %\usepackage{longtable}<br>&gt; %\usepackage{cite}<br>&gt; %\usepackage{natbib}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; \include{GrandMacros}<br>&gt; \include{ColourMacros}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; enewcommand{	hesection}{\Roman{section}}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; 
ewcommand{ eno}{ egin{eqnarray}}<br>&gt; 
ewcommand{\eno}{\end{eqnarray}}<br>&gt; 
ewcommand{ enone}{ egin{eqnarray*}}<br>&gt; 
ewcommand{\enone}{\end{eqnarray*}}<br>&gt; \usepackage{url}<br>&gt; \setlength{	opmargin}{-.5in}<br>&gt; \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{0.0in}<br>&gt; \setlength{\evensidemargin}{0.0in}<br>&gt; \setlength{	extwidth}{6.6in}<br>&gt; \setlength{	extheight}{9in}<br>&gt; \setlength{\parindent}{0in}<br>&gt; \setlength{\parskip}{2ex}<br>&gt; \setlength{ aselineskip}{12pt}<br>&gt;<br>&gt; 
